Page 1 of 4

Pita-Pan ties his blue rope and hopes to reach the summit before the evening light turns
gold. Today he wants to prove he can climb alone.
Page 2 of 4

On a narrow ledge, he finds a younger goat frozen with fear. The quickest path continues
upward, but Pita anchors the rope beside her.
Page 3 of 4

Inside a cold cloud, they cannot see the trail. Pita asks his new partner to listen for the
bell at the peak, and she leads by sound.
Page 4 of 4

They reach the summit as the valley glows below. Pita did not prove he could climb alone;
he discovered how far two careful climbers can go.
Questions for Pita-Pan’s Mountain Climb

Read the story together first. Use one question at each page, then the question at the end. Answers are below
the dotted line: fold them under or cover them while reading.
Page 1

Talk together: What does Pita-Pan want to prove?
Page 2
Talk together: What choice does Pita make on the ledge?
Page 3
Talk together: How does the younger goat help in the cloud?
Page 4
Talk together: How has Pita’s idea of success changed?
After reading
Why did Pita-Pan stop on the ledge?
Answers (fold under before reading)

After reading: To help a frightened younger goat.

